"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 14847, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017g3CnNVs3yecpef7zjeqzj", "tool": "commit_changes", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 14847, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017g3CnNVs3yecpef7zjeqzj", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18024, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01T4kK4XkPrWsgqtFV9FCgPJ", "tool": "trigger_ci", "args": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 18324, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01T4kK4XkPrWsgqtFV9FCgPJ", "tool": "trigger_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18324, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01T4kK4XkPrWsgqtFV9FCgPJ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 21017, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01QdcKPVYKcTDqdLeJ7MKqmZ", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "args": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 378324, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QdcKPVYKcTDqdLeJ7MKqmZ", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 378324, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QdcKPVYKcTDqdLeJ7MKqmZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 386921, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01MsfMM29tKi3tiN3NNJCF7f", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\nFixes the failing nightly build. `round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, so `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed (e.g. `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\n## Change\n- Switch the import and `quantize` rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: passed.\n\nNote: this changes the rounding result for exact half-cent amounts whose preceding digit is even (they now round down instead of up). This matches FIN-212, but anything downstream that relied on the old half-up behavior should be checked.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 387821, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MsfMM29tKi3tiN3NNJCF7f", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 387821, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MsfMM29tKi3tiN3NNJCF7f", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 5122819, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** The comment in `src/money.py` says `round_money` uses banker's rounding (round half to even), but the code actually rounded halves up. That's why `2.665` became `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to round half to even. It's a one-line change plus the matching import (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nFIN-212 isn't in the security advisory lookup, so it's probably an internal ticket. I went by the test and the code comment instead. The PR description notes that amounts ending in exactly half a cent with an even digit before it now round down instead of up. Anything that depended on the old behaviour should be checked.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the repository and the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XW1aBgSoEnX4gyeggR2Fmz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01F9qKnT2bCZ5XUYiT84rF4g", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016yWogjEefs5vaE9ssDtJeE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GT9pzFuMX4BrEFVHXUjJYW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.7}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01K6MbwomoVnopyrCHtxKzC3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017g3CnNVs3yecpef7zjeqzj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01T4kK4XkPrWsgqtFV9FCgPJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QdcKPVYKcTDqdLeJ7MKqmZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on 08d3cd5986. Opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MsfMM29tKi3tiN3NNJCF7f", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\nFixes the failing nightly build. `round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, so `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed (e.g. `2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\n## Change\n- Switch the import and `quantize` rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: passed.\n\nNote: this changes the rounding result for exact half-cent amounts whose preceding digit is even (they now round down instead of up). This matches FIN-212, but anything downstream that relied on the old half-up behavior should be checked.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** The comment in `src/money.py` says `round_money` uses banker's rounding (round half to even), but the code actually rounded halves up. That's why `2.665` became `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to round half to even. It's a one-line change plus the matching import (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nFIN-212 isn't in the security advisory lookup, so it's probably an internal ticket. I went by the test and the code comment instead. The PR description notes that amounts ending in exactly half a cent with an even digit before it now round down instead of up. Anything that depended on the old behaviour should be checked.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}